# NOTE: do NOT re-add a broad `/docs` ignore. It was introduced in 1f83cd3 to
# keep then-local hardening notes untracked, but it silently ignored every NEW
# file under docs/ (runbooks, design sources) while the already-tracked ones
# stayed tracked (a trap). Nothing under docs/ is generated output; if a
# generator ever lands, ignore its exact output subdirectory only.
# NOTE: do NOT re-add a broad `content/` ignore either. It claimed the lesson
# MDX was authored locally and untracked, which stopped being true: 210 files
# live under content/ in git - 192 lessons, 16 final-exam quizzes and the two
# READMEs - and content/README.md calls the folder the source of truth for the
# catalogue. The rule matched none of them, because git ignores nothing it
# already tracks, so it did exactly one thing: silently drop every NEW lesson
# from `git add`. Same trap as the `/docs` rule above, and it had not bitten
# only because no lesson had been added since. Nothing under content/ is
# generated output.

# design-sync: local design tooling workspace (kept on disk, never committed)
.ds-sync/
ds-bundle/
.design-sync/

# Local-only working docs and dev tooling (kept on disk, not tracked in the repo)
/CLAUDE.md
/CyberLearn.md
/CyberLearn_Patch_ImportLessons.md
/.agents/
/skills-lock.json
